# The worker's two secrets, both optional: a private wiki without backups needs neither (setup 2.1).
# They're entered in the dashboard, under the worker's Settings → Variables and Secrets, as the type
# Secret (setup 2.5); the Deploy to Cloudflare button asks for them, reading this file. A local run
# (`npx wrangler dev`) reads them from a copy of this file named .dev.vars, which git ignores. No
# value goes in this file, ever: it's part of the repository.

# A fine-grained personal access token limited to the backup repository, with Contents: read and
# write (setup 2.4). Pairs with the GITHUB_REPO variable; without both, no backups.
GITHUB_TOKEN=

# An API token with Zone → Cache Purge on the public site's zone (setup 2.5), for the public site's
# purges; pairs with the CF_ZONE_ID variable. Public site only; without both, no purges.
CF_API_TOKEN=
